The commit introduces the `reserve_unaccepted()` function which contains the vulnerability. Specifically, in lines 644-645, it calculates the start and size as:

	start = PAGE_ALIGN_DOWN(efi.unaccepted);
	size = PAGE_ALIGN(sizeof(*unaccepted) + unaccepted->size);

If `efi.unaccepted` is not page-aligned, `start` is rounded down, but `size` is calculated only based on the table size without accounting for the offset (`efi.unaccepted - start`). This can result in the end of the table being left unreserved.
